  "worked_solution": "Let $u=x-2.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$x=u+2.$\n\nNow we can solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (u+2)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int {u}^{3/2}+2{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}+\\frac{4}{3}{u}^{3/2})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{5}}+\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt{(x-2)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
